\title{Scott and Wilmer: Combinatorics in the exterior algebra and the Bollobás Two Families Theorem}
\taxon{Reference}
\tag{bibliography}
\meta{dependencies}{None.}
\meta{provenance}{Bibliographic details checked against the publisher; mathematical comparison based on arXiv:1907.06019v2, 14 July 2020, read on 12 October 2026.}

\p{Alex Scott and Elizabeth Wilmer. \em{Combinatorics in the exterior algebra and the Bollobás Two Families Theorem}. Journal of the London Mathematical Society 104(4) (2021), 1812–1839. [Publisher and DOI](https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms.12484). [Version read](https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.06019v2); [full text](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1907.06019v2).}

\p{The relevant parts are Section 2.1 on initial monomials, Lemma 3.1 on generic projections, and Theorem 4.5 on weighted subspace pairs. Numbered locators here refer to the linked preprint version. [The comparison](cn-0072) explains their relation to [the subspace-intersection inequality](cn-0024). Lemma 3.1 also yields [an ambient-dimension refinement](cn-0074).}
